{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type Updater<TInput, TOutput> = TOutput | ((input: TInput) => TOutput);","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L103","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:103"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Either a plain value of type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"},{"type":"text","value":", or a function that receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TInput"},{"type":"text","value":" and returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"},{"type":"text","value":".\nUsed for example by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setQueryData"},{"type":"text","value":"-style updaters, which accept either the new data directly or a\nfunction that computes it from the previous data. See functionalUpdate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tinput","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TInput"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TInput"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toutput","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TOutput"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], newPosts)\n\n// Or, using an updater function that receives the current data:\nqueryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], (oldPosts) =>\n  oldPosts ? [...oldPosts, newPost] : oldPosts,\n)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tinput","text":"TInput","level":3},{"id":"toutput","text":"TOutput","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype Updater<TInput, TOutput> = TOutput | ((input: TInput) => TOutput);\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:103](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L103)\n\nEither a plain value of type `TOutput`, or a function that receives `TInput` and returns `TOutput`.\nUsed for example by `setQueryData`-style updaters, which accept either the new data directly or a\nfunction that computes it from the previous data. See functionalUpdate.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TInput\n\n`TInput`\n\n### TOutput\n\n`TOutput`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], newPosts)\n\n// Or, using an updater function that receives the current data:\nqueryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], (oldPosts) =>\n  oldPosts ? [...oldPosts, newPost] : oldPosts,\n)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: Updater\ntitle: Updater\n---\n\n```ts\ntype Updater<TInput, TOutput> = TOutput | ((input: TInput) => TOutput);\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:103](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L103)\n\nEither a plain value of type `TOutput`, or a function that receives `TInput` and returns `TOutput`.\nUsed for example by `setQueryData`-style updaters, which accept either the new data directly or a\nfunction that computes it from the previous data. See functionalUpdate.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TInput\n\n`TInput`\n\n### TOutput\n\n`TOutput`\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], newPosts)\n\n// Or, using an updater function that receives the current data:\nqueryClient.setQueryData(['posts'], (oldPosts) =>\n  oldPosts ? [...oldPosts, newPost] : oldPosts,\n)\n```\n"}
